<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell 0.3-pct gas oil for end-Apr.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell 0.3-pct gas oil for end-Apr.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan' state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 225,000-250,000 barrels of 0.3-percent sulphur gas oil for April 21-30 lifting, a CPC source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The cargo is to be lifted from Kaohsiung, free-on-board (fob) basis.</p>
<p>The tender closes on March 12 and offers will be valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold two gas oil cargoes at around $25.60 per barrel for March 1-12 lifting fob Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
